<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sudak</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Soldaia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sudak is a town on the south-east coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>. As Soldaia it was a major trading port from the Byzantine era; it was attacked by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> around 1222 and by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>, and Venetian merchants kept a consulate there. The Genoese took it in 1365 and built its fortress, which survives, before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> captured it in 1475.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sudak.jpg" alt="Sudak" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vyacheslav Argenberg · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sudak,_Crimea.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
